Guardian links: resolve guardian_erp_name on sibling-roster copy

When a new sibling is added (via /admin/data/students/.../guardians or
.../sibling-student), the route copies the source sibling's
student_guardian_links rows verbatim. Legacy/orphan links from earlier
code paths carry guardian_erp_name = NULL, and copying them verbatim
propagates the NULL forever. /admin/guardians joins linked students by
erp_name, so every NULL-linked sibling is silently invisible — that's
why a guardian with 6 linked students was showing only 2.

Fix: COALESCE the source's guardian_erp_name with a phone-match lookup
into guardians.mobile_number on copy. If a guardian master exists for
that phone, the new link gets its erp_name and surfaces correctly; if
no master exists, the NULL passes through (no master to attach to).

Idempotent — re-runs of the heal SQL or this route never write a
worse value.

